OL,3,AHow colourful stripes (and rubber
OL,4,Achickens) helped Paul Smith conquer the
OL,5,Afashion world
OL,6,
OL,7,FSir Paul Smith, the doyen of British
OL,8,Ffashion, is flailing around in his
OL,9,Foffice with two large rubber chickens
OL,10,Fand making them squeak them with gusto.
OL,12,F"The chickens are the reason I was
OL,13,Fsuccessful in Japan," he explains.
OL,15,F"I've been working in Japan since 1982.
OL,16,FAnd when I first went there, there was
OL,17,Fone person who spoke schoolboy English.
OL,18,FSo, it was very much about
OL,19,Fcommunicating through gesture,
OL,20,Fdrawings, but also humour."
OL,22,FEnter the rubber chickens.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/19
